{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Everyday Things"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "What Time Does She Have Breakfast? "}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 4}, {"type": "level", "content": "Beginner"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Daily Routines"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Routines</span>  are things you do in order.   Your <span class=\"strong\">daily routines</span>  are the actions you do every day. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Let's look at some examples."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":1,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"wake up/get up <br />eat breakfast/lunch/dinner <br />walk  <br />drive <br />do \u2026 <br />study <br />cook <br />watch <br />go to school/work/bed\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I wake up at 6 a.m. <br />I eat lunch at noon. <br />She walks to school.  <br />He drives to work. <br />We do our homework after school. <br />He studies in the library. <br />My mom cooks dinner at 5 p.m. <br />After dinner, they watch TV. <br />You go to bed at 11 p.m. </span> \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Note: You use the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Present tense </span> to talk about routines."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to wake up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to stop sleeping"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I wake up in the morning at 6 o'clock."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn1le04ob05aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about 